GEO:39.169199;-86.515674
SUMMARY:Black Sea Security Lecture: "Russia in Europe and the Middle East
 : Two Theaters\, One Strategy" with Iulia Joja
DESCRIPTION:Russia's convergence with Iran — shared targeting data\, dr
 one shipments\, sanctions evasion — links the Black Sea to the Strait o
 f Hormuz\, yet NATO still treats these as separate theatres. As Senator R
 ichard Lugar warned in 1993\, "NATO will either develop a strategy and st
 ructure to go 'out of area' or it will 'go out of business.'" This talk a
 rgues Russia's challenges demand one integrated transatlantic strategy.  
 Iulia Joja is a senior fellow at the Middle East Institute\, where she fo
 cuses on the intersection between Europe and the Middle East. She is also
  an adjunct professor at Georgetown University and George Washington Univ
 ersity\, teaching European security.Cosponsored by The Byrnes Institute (
 REEI)\, the Jean Monnet Chair\, and the Center for the Study of the Middl
 e East
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Russia's convergence with Iran — shar
 ed targeting data\, drone shipments\, sanctions evasion — links the Bla
 ck Sea to the Strait of Hormuz\, yet NATO still treats these as separate 
 theatres. As Senator Richard Lugar warned in 1993\, "NATO will either dev
 elop a strategy and structure to go 'out of area' or it will 'go out of b
 usiness.'" This talk argues Russia's challenges demand one integrated tra
 nsatlantic strategy.</p><p>  Iulia Joja is a senior fellow at the Middle 
 East Institute\, where she focuses on the intersection between Europe and
  the Middle East. She is also an adjunct professor at Georgetown Universi
 ty and George Washington University\, teaching European security.</p><p><
 em>Cosponsored by The Byrnes Institute (REEI)\, the Jean Monnet Chair\, a
 nd the Center for the Study of the Middle East</em></p>
