SUMMARY:The one thing you need to know about climate change
DESCRIPTION:Come join moderator Nikos Zirogiannis (https://oneill.indiana
 .edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/zirogiannis-ni
 kolaos.html) (O'Neill School) and five other IUB faculty members as they 
 share the one thing you need to know about climate change.Christopher Cal
 lahan (https://oneill.indiana.edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/fac
 ulty/full-time/callahan-christopher.html) (O'Neill)\, Rebecca Dirksen (ht
 tps://folklore.indiana.edu/about/faculty/dirksen-rebecca.html) (Folklore 
 &amp\; Ethnomusicology)\, Sara Gregg (https://history.indiana.edu/faculty
 _staff/faculty/gregg_sara.html) (History)\, Kim Novick (https://oneill.in
 diana.edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/novick-ki
 mberly.html) (O'Neill and ESSI (https://environment.indiana.edu/index.htm
 l))\, and Spencer Perry (https://education.indiana.edu/news/2026/jul-dec/
 2026-08-20-iusoe-welcomes-new-faculty.html) (School of Education) will ea
 ch share five minutes of what they want us to know about climate change. 
  These talks will be followed by discussion and Q&amp\;A. This event is s
 ponsored by IU's Institute for Advanced Study (https://ias.indiana.edu/).
  All IU and Bloomington community members are invited to attend and learn
  with us during this IU Climate Week (https://eri.iu.edu/news-and-events/
 events/iu-climate-week.html) event.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Come join moderator <a href="https://on
 eill.indiana.edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/zi
 rogiannis-nikolaos.html">Nikos Zirogiannis</a> (O'Neill School) and five 
 other IUB faculty members as they share the one thing you need to know ab
 out climate change.</p><p><a href="https://oneill.indiana.edu/faculty-res
 earch/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/callahan-christopher.html">Chr
 istopher Callahan</a> (O'Neill)\, <a href="https://folklore.indiana.edu/a
 bout/faculty/dirksen-rebecca.html">Rebecca Dirksen</a> (Folklore &amp\; E
 thnomusicology)\, <a href="https://history.indiana.edu/faculty_staff/facu
 lty/gregg_sara.html">Sara Gregg</a> (History)\, <a href="https://oneill.i
 ndiana.edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/novick-k
 imberly.html">Kim Novick</a> (O'Neill and <a href="https://environment.in
 diana.edu/index.html">ESSI</a>)\, and <a href="https://education.indiana.
 edu/news/2026/jul-dec/2026-08-20-iusoe-welcomes-new-faculty.html">Spencer
  Perry</a> (School of Education) will each share five minutes of what the
 y want us to know about climate change.</p><p>  These talks will be follo
 wed by discussion and Q&amp\;A. This event is sponsored by IU's <a href="
 https://ias.indiana.edu/">Institute for Advanced Study</a>. All IU and Bl
 oomington community members are invited to attend and learn with us durin
 g this <a href="https://eri.iu.edu/news-and-events/events/iu-climate-week
 .html">IU Climate Week</a> event.</p>
